Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='remotebuilder', at=datetime(2026, 9, 13, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title="x86_64 derivations build on a Codespace remote builder; crane's dependency builds are rooted per system", body="*A remote builder, and two rooted dependency builds* (2026-09-13). The box's daemon ships x86\\_64-linux derivations to a Codespace (`nix-builder`, made from an empty PERSONAL repository — never an org's — reached through gh's ssh transport; the nixos config repository says how). This box is aarch64, so the builder takes the APK and the checks (`nix build .#checks.x86_64-linux.suzatary-core`; warm clippy 37 s there against 981 s for a local `flake check`), never the ARM binary. Crane's dependency build is a build-time input nothing roots, and the daemon collects below 3 GB free, so it is rooted per architecture: `nix build -o ~/.local/state/suzatary/roots/deps-<system> .#suzatary-deps` (and `.#packages.x86_64-linux.suzatary-deps`). Only a lock change rebuilds them; re-run those two after one. Never `--no-link` a build whose artifacts should survive the next collection.", rationale='Decided 2026-09-13. Measured: warm clippy 37 s on the builder against 981 s for a local flake check.', supersedes=()))